    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d533">

                <pb facs="0762" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg750"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Japan)/10–1245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Political Adviser in Japan</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-12">October 12,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received November 6—6 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>41. Reference our 31, October 10. Prince Konoye has been attached by the Emperor
                    to the office of the Lord Keeper of the Privy Seal<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d533-f1"/> for the purpose of undertaking studies leading to the
                    thorough revision of the Constitution.</p>
                <p>We have been privately informed that the Prince will be assisted by
                    constitutional experts and that he desired to keep in close contact with us
                    during the progress of the work, submitting the draft article by article for our
                    advice and the consideration of General MacArthur.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d533-f1" n="41" xml:id="d533-f1-content">
                <p>Marquis Koicho Kido.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
